				<div class="post-655 post hentry category-software-reviews">
			<h2 id="post-655"><a href="http://blog.cromwellhaus.com/index.php/2006/03/windows-live-messenger-beta-update/" rel="bookmark" title="Permanent Link to Windows Live Messenger Beta Update">Windows Live Messenger Beta Update</a></h2>
			<small class="meta">March 6th, 2006 </small>

			<div class="entry">
				<p>This week the Windows Live group released an update to the <A href="http://ideas.live.com/programPage.aspx?versionId=0eccd94b-eb48-497c-8e60-c6313f7ebb73" mce_href="http://ideas.live.com/programPage.aspx?versionId=0eccd94b-eb48-497c-8e60-c6313f7ebb73">Windows Live Messenger Beta</A> (MSN Messenger 8.0). There were a couple of major things with the initial release <A class="" href="http://www.cromwellhaus.com/blogs/ryanc/archive/2006/01/13/36.aspx" mce_href="http://www.cromwellhaus.com/blogs/ryanc/archive/2006/01/13/36.aspx">that I reported</A> and they seem to have been resolved. If you&#8217;d like to give it a chance, I have a few new invites that I can give out to those who are interested and I&#8217;m sure I&#8217;ll receive some more shortly thereafter. Leave your email in the comments and I&#8217;ll do my best.</p>
			</div>

